<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	NOTE TO EDITORS

	RoR is built with plain CMake rather than Xcode, so nothing supplies an
	entitlements file at all.  This deliberately EMPTY dictionary exists only
	so that codesign embeds an entitlements blob together with its DER form,
	exactly the way the one bundle in this repository that is known to
	install was signed (the milestone-0 smoke test, whose entitlements file
	is an empty dict too).

	A free Apple ID cannot carry extra entitlements, so there is nothing to
	put in here.  The signatures that actually authorise the app are added by
	whoever sideloads the IPA.

	The flags, in words: sign ad-hoc, attach this entitlements file, and
	generate the DER form of the entitlements.

	DO NOT put two consecutive hyphens in this comment.  XML forbids that
	sequence inside a comment, and the entitlements parser built into the
	operating system rejects the whole file if it sees one.  The previous
	revision of this file did exactly that and codesign answered:

	    Failed to parse entitlements: AMFIUnserializeXML:
	    syntax error near line 9

	which left the bundle completely unsigned and is what started this whole
	investigation.  A plain XML parser rejects the file the same way, which
	is how it was confirmed on a machine with no macOS on it.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
